air fryers have become super popular the  last few years  they're great because they're energy  efficient they cook foods fast  and they're really easy to use i mean  you can cook just about  anything in them from beautifully brown  vegetables to crispy skin chicken wings  even lightenery cakes it only takes a  small amount of oil  to cook delicious food today we're going  to be focusing on air frying  savory foods tasty 101 air fryers  so what is an air fryer first of all  they're ovens  not fryers they're basically these mini  powerful conduction ovens their key  element  is having fans that blow hot air in  circulation  so the temperature is equalized  throughout the oven this hot air  circulation surrounds the food  cooking it evenly and quickly because of  this air fryers require  little to no oil compared to deep frying  while there are many air fryers on the  market  they generally fall into two categories  basket air fryers and convection oven  air fryers  the basket air fryers are the most  popular with a basket  similar to a deep fryer to hold the food  both will achieve similar results  before we get started here are some  basic tips to keep in mind no matter  what you're cooking  it's important that you give your  machine enough space on all sides to  account for proper airflow  a good rule of thumb is to allow five  inches of clearance on all sides  and make sure your surfaces are heat  proof you don't want to cook with an air  fryer that's pushed against a wall  always have the grate in the basket this  allows hot air to circulate around the  food  and also keeps the food from sitting in  excess oil if you have a wire rack for  your air fryer  use it it helps the food stay crispy on  the bottom  really takes things to the next level  just trust us  it's always good to preheat the air  fryer for about two to three minutes and  then you're good to go  it's also helpful to use a non-aerosol  oil spray to help prevent sticking  and to keep your foods nice and crispy  now we're going to go over four popular  foods you'll cook in an air fryer  foods with a dry batter foods with the  wet batter  batterless foods and frozen foods our  first recipe is going to be a dry batter  with coconut shrimp we have a little  secret to the perfect shrimp  that secret is buttermilk we're going to  marinate the shrimp and buttermilk for  30 minutes  this helps to tenderize the shrimp so  they don't overcook in the air fryer  this technique also works great for  chicken pork or even steaks  but first we need to season the shrimp  in a small bowl we're going to stir  together the salt  pepper garlic powder and paprika we're  going to place the shrimp on a cutting  board and pat dry with paper towels  then we'll season the shrimp on both  sides with our spice mixture  we're using jumbo shrimp that's been  peeled and deveined the bigger the  shrimp the better to prevent overcooking  we'll add our seasoned shrimp to a bowl  with the buttermilk and lime zest  then we're going to let it marinate for  about 30 minutes we're using lime zest  to go with the caribbean coconut theme  but feel free to emit if you don't have  them  now we're going to preheat the air fryer  to 380 degrees fahrenheit  we have our flour eggs and panko in  three separate bowls  now we're going to add the coconut  flakes to the bread crumbs and we'll  stir it to combine  you can also substitute panko with bread  crumbs chips pretzels or crackers  now we're gonna remove the shrimp from  the marinade and we'll gently shake it  to get off any excess buttermilk  we're simply coating the shrimp in a  thin layer of flour and shaking off any  of the excess  next we'll dip the floured shrimp into  the beaten egg wash  make sure the eggs are really well  beaten so it evenly coats the shrimp  this helps the main coating stick to the  food for our final step  breading now we'll dredge it once again  into the panko mixture  we're going to add half the shrimp to  the airfryer so it's not overcrowded  we'll spray it with the non-aerosol  oil spray and cook for about three  minutes then  we're gonna flip spray the tops and cook  for another one to two minutes or until  they're nice and crispy  if the shrimp's tail is pink that's a  good sign it's cooked now let's remove  them from the basket and repeat with our  remaining shrimp  it's important not to overcrowd your air  fryer you don't want the shrimp to steam  you want it to get real crispy now serve  it with your favorite dipping sauce and  some lime wedges  this dredge method works for onion rings  mozzarella sticks  chicken nuggets chicken tenders avocado  fries  zucchini fries let your creativity take  over and dredge away  for our wet batter recipe we're going to  air fry buffalo cauliflower wings  first we'll preheat the air fryer to 430  degrees fahrenheit for about five  minutes  now we noticed that our different air  fryers go up to different temperatures  so you might just have to keep an eye on  it and maybe your food needs to cook for  a little bit longer  now we're gonna mix together our cake  flour corn starch  baking powder smoked paprika garlic  powder  onion powder and a half teaspoon of salt  we're using cake flour because it has a  lower protein content which prevents a  bready crust  you might also notice we're not using  eggs in this wet batter  that's because when we tested it it  resulted in a cakey batter and to be  honest it wasn't that great  now slowly stir in the sparkling water  when sparkling water is added to a  batter  its bubbles create pockets of air that  give the final product a beautiful light  texture  once again the most important part of  this is in the mixing  when combining the ingredients do not  over mix the batter  it is also vital to prepare the batter  right before cooking  this gives the flour as little time as  possible to soak up water  giving you maximum crispiness now we're  going to toss the cauliflower florets  with the remaining corn starch and salt  cauliflower releases water when it's  cooked and that can lead to a soggy  crust  the corn starch catches that water and  prevents it from ruining the batter  this will help you get that beautiful  golden color and classic crunchiness  make sure to shake off any excess  cornstarch then dip into the wet batter  and let any excess drip off place the  cauliflower in a single layer and cook  for about five minutes or until nice and  golden brown work in batches  and remember never overcrowd the  airfryer with too much food  once nice and golden brown remove the  cauliflower from the air fryer and  repeat with the remaining florets  while your cauliflower is cooking let's  make the sauce we're gonna mix together  some hot sauce  butter and honey and we're gonna cook it  stirring it occasionally  until it's just heated through the  butter is melted and it's evenly  combined  now let's toss the cauliflower wings  with the buffalo sauce and enjoy  immediately no really it's actually the  best eaten right away or it can get too  soggy  this method works with any kind of  vegetable or protein sweet potatoes  asparagus  green beans no batter no problem  balsamic chicken thighs to the rescue  start by generously seasoning the  chicken thighs with salt on both sides  and make sure to go under the skin  there's nothing worse than under  seasoned food seriously  don't be alarmed by the amount of salt  we're about to use then whisk together  the dijon  balsamic olive oil garlic powder and  italian seasoning  we're going to add the seasoned chicken  thighs to the marinade and toss to coat  them completely  then we'll cover and refrigerate for at  least four hours but preferably  overnight let the chicken come to room  temperature before you start cooking  preheat the air fryer to 380 degrees  fahrenheit for about three minutes  now we'll remove the chicken from our  marinade and we'll pat them dry with  paper towels  this will help get the chicken super  crispy adding a spritz of non-aerosol  cooking spray or a drizzle of olive oil  to your food before air frying will give  you nice browning and crispiness  add as many chicken thighs as will fit  skin side down and cook for five to  seven minutes  we're cooking the chicken thighs skin  side down so the skin can start to  render the fat without browning the skin  too much  flip the chicken so the skin side is up  and cook for an additional  five to seven minutes until the internal  temperature reaches 165 degrees  fahrenheit  repeat with any remaining chicken thighs  if you need to this method can also be  done with buffalo chicken wings  meatballs salmon whole roasted chicken  or steak there may be no batter in this  method but it is a  home run now here are some quick tips  for air frying frozen foods  because of the popularity of the air  fryer some frozen foods now conveniently  have instructions for using the  appliance right on the package  but if they don't the rule of thumb is  to use the same temperature as you would  in an oven  but cut the cooking time in half so if  the instructions on the package  recommend 20 minutes at 400 degrees you  should only cook it for about 10 minutes  at 400 degrees in an air fryer give the  basket nice shimmy and shake halfway  through the cooking to redistribute the  food  and give it a chance to brown and crisp  up evenly in general  we found that foods fried in the  airfryer are significantly better when  eaten while hot  they tend to harden up a bit as they  cool much like foods cooked in more  traditional ways  but in a more pronounced way now here's  some quick reminders and cleaning tips  remember that with air fryers food cooks  way faster than you're used to it's one  of its best attributes  you can reference your fryer's manual  but in general the less food in the  basket the shorter the cook time will be  the more food the longer it will be it's  pretty straightforward  by the way if you're trying to figure  out sizing here's a quick cheat sheet  in general if you're cooking for more  people you should invest in a bigger  frying basket  but if you're cooking solo just invest  in something small if you're cooking  greasy food in your air fryer  don't be surprised if you see some smoke  don't stress it  just place a slice of bread in the  bottom of the unit to soak up any excess  grease  clean the basket after every use just  with some soap and water and a gentle  sponge  it's a non-stick cooking surface so you  don't want to use a scratchy sponge  if you have any hard to clean stuck on  messes just sprinkle with baking soda  and let it sit for like five minutes  then use a sponge to wipe it clean so  next time you're thinking of reheating  food in the microwave  how about using the air fryer for crispy  and tasty leftovers  there you have it air fryers are pretty  versatile and easy to use  i hope that this has been helpful to you  and maybe give one of these recipes a  fry  [Music]  you
 

